  - libeuicc (src/main/jni/lpac/euicc) is from lpac by ESTKME TECHNOLOGY LIMITED,
    LGPL-2.1-only OR LicenseRef-ESTKME-Commercial; used here under LGPL-2.1-only.
    Licences: src/main/jni/lpac/LICENSES/, src/main/jni/lpac/REUSE.toml.
  - lpac's cjson-ext is MIT (src/main/jni/lpac/LICENSES/MIT.txt).
  - euicc/sha256.c and sha256.h are Brad Conte's crypto-algorithms, CC0-1.0.
  - cJSON (src/main/jni/cjson/cjson) by Dave Gamble and cJSON contributors, MIT.
    Licence: src/main/jni/cjson/cjson/LICENSE.

android/app/src/main/assets/sounds/, installer/croissant/sounds/, android/app/src/main/assets/metronome/
  The interface sound packs and their demos, and the metronome's Tine, Chime and Bamboo,
  rendered by sounds/earshot.py and sounds/metronome.py with
  earshot (https://github.com/Leonxlnx/earshot) by Leon Lin, MIT: its bank of sounds
  stored as code and its DSP. Three of the bank's sounds are models fitted from CC0
  recordings on Freesound: Bamboo hit by michorvath (fs-386888), Keychron k10 keys by
  Sadiquecat (fs-789628) and Switch Flip #1 by IanStarGem (fs-278205).

android/app/src/main/assets/sounds/zen/, installer/croissant/sounds/zen.m4a
  The Zen pack of uisfx (https://github.com/uisfx), the audio CC0, uisfx's code MIT;
